# Character Page Conventions

When creating, editing, or auditing character pages in `content/characters/`:

## 1. Mandatory Character Picture
Every character page MUST include an authentic screencap picture directly beneath the primary `# Character Name` heading:

```markdown
# Character Name

![Character Name on Barely Informed News](https://github.com/trak3r/binlore/releases/download/media-assets/<character-slug>.jpg)
```

### Screencap Extraction & Upload Workflow:
1. Extract a clear frame showing the character from their VOD appearance using `binlore screencap` or `tools/binlore_tools/screencap.py` via `ffmpeg`.
2. Save the screencap locally to `tools/screencaps/<character-slug>.jpg`.
3. Upload the asset to GitHub release `media-assets` on repository `trak3r/binlore`:
   ```bash
   gh release upload media-assets --repo trak3r/binlore tools/screencaps/<character-slug>.jpg --clobber
   ```
4. Embed the URL `https://github.com/trak3r/binlore/releases/download/media-assets/<character-slug>.jpg` right under the `# Name` heading.

## 2. Required Structure & Cross-Links
- Frontmatter (`title`, `type: character`, `aliases`, `first_seen`, `status`, `tags: [character, ...]`).
- `# Name` + Image embed directly under heading.
- Overview & Persona.
- Detailed character lore, relationships, backstory, and signature bits.
- `## Appearances` table linking to episodes.
- `## Notable Quotes` and `## Notable Moments`.
- `## Open Questions`.
- `See also:` linking to relevant segments, storylines, or index.
- Always add/update the character's row in `content/characters/index.md`.
